> Also, have you tested larger max depth numbers? Is this the absolute maximum values we can use?

@astefan that's not the highest limit we can reach, 1000 is still good for a unit test, but not for all the scenarios in a real deploy (see the failure you identified at ~1923, and consider that you have to account for commands + expressions) where the stack is much deeper. 
500 is the best "round" threshold that gives us enough guarantees; in the future, if there is a real need, raising it will be much less problematic than lowering it.
